   "id": "01#s07",
   "type": "section",
   "lesson": "01",
   "href": "lessons/01-cache-redis.html#s07",
   "title": "Five lines worth stealing",
   "subtitle": "Lesson 01 · Take away",
   "text": "\"How much of your evening peak is people looking, not people paying?\" Splits one vague complaint into two different problems with two very different price tags. People looking is a cache problem. People paying is a core problem. Most vendors quote the expensive one by default. \"We are not replacing your core. We are stopping it from being asked the same question two million times a day.\" Protects the decision they already made and paid for, instead of attacking it. You are adding a layer in front, not proposing a migration nobody asked for. \"Nothing in the payment approval reads from a copy. What we show and what we approve are two different risks.\" The sentence that gets you past the risk committee. Say it before they ask, not after. \"How do you handle a customer tapping Transfer twice on a bad connection today?\" Money leaving twice is a headline risk at any retail bank, and almost nobody in a sales meeting asks about it. Ask it and you stop being a vendor. \"If it holds login sessions and OTP codes, it holds personal data — let's put that on the agenda now, not in the security review.\" Phone numbers, session records and OTPs are personal data under Nghị định 13/2023, and the bank's security assessment will ask where those servers physically sit. Raising it yourself is worth more than answering it late. Tiếng Việt Dùng nguyên văn tiếng Anh khi làm việc với C-level ngân hàng. Ý cốt lõi: đừng bán tốc độ. Bán việc gỡ tải khỏi core, số tiền khách hoãn được nhờ đó, và ranh giới rủi ro mà bạn chủ động nêu trước khi họ hỏi.",
